    "result_text": "All tests pass. `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0`.\n\n## Summary\n\nReleased version 2 of the owner identity with minimal, cohesive changes across the four areas the spec calls out.\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 tag mixed in, so every identifier changes):**\n- `MemberId.of` \u2014 region segment is now `\"V2\" + region` (e.g. `V2NSW\u2026`), so the tag lives *inside* the memberId.\n- `MemberId.region` \u2014 strips the leading `\"V2\"` when reading it back, so any consumer deriving from the identity gets the *plain* region.\n- `HouseholdId.of` / `IdentityKey.of` \u2014 prepend the constant `\"V2|\"` to their hash inputs. Because the tag is constant across all owners, every value changes but duplicate-detection/household-grouping comparisons still hold.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` \u2192 regenerated DTOs):\n- Removed top-level `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`; added a nested `Identity` schema holding all three, exposed as `identity`, plus a top-level integer `apiVersion`.\n- `OwnerMapper` gains a small `toIdentity(owner)` builder and two mappings (`identity`, `apiVersion = 2`). `IdentityKey` was made `public` so the mapper can build the full object once \u2014 which also means list/page responses now carry identity consistently. The two responders just drop their now-obsolete `setIdentityKey` line.\n\n**Audit event** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 bumped to schema version 2: added `\"schemaVersion\":2` and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the v2 identity (`MemberId.region` yields the plain region \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`).\n\n**Kept plain (no V2 tag):** `locality`, `timezone`, and both owner-segment derivations \u2014 the tag only ever appears inside the three identifiers. Request fields are untouched.\n\nVerified in the run: `memberId=V2NSW2616E6609E9`, audit line `{\"schemaVersion\":2,\u2026,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\u2026}`, and the acceptance test's structural contract (grouped `identity`, `apiVersion` 2, no top-level identifiers).",
