    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and implemented in the `function/owner/*` classes. Every step runs under a single `transaction` governance that commits once at the end.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Without that role the request is rejected (403) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## Ordered steps\n\n**1. `checkIdempotent` \u2014 `CheckIdempotencyKey`** *(guard)*\nReads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was already seen **and** the owner it created still exists, it short-circuits with **200 OK** returning the original owner \u2014 no new owner is created. Otherwise it takes the `proceed` flow. (The `SEEN` map is static and survives rollback by design.)\n\n**2. `build` \u2014 `BuildOwner`** *(validation + side-effects)*\n- Bean-validates the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (failures \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, 400):\n  - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, letters pattern `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`, size 1\u201330\n  - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, letters pattern (optional trailing `.`), size 1\u201330\n  - `city`: `@NotNull`, non-blank, size 1\u201380\n  - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, size 1\u201320\n  - `title`: size \u226410; `address`: non-blank if present, size 1\u2013255; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`: size \u2264255; `email`: `@Email`, size \u2264255\n- Maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` (id/pets ignored).\n- If `registrationDate` is null \u2192 **defaults it to today**; if it is after today \u2192 throws `RegistrationDateInFutureException` (400).\n- Publishes the `Owner` and the `OwnerFieldsDto` as pipeline variables.\n\n**3. `ensureEmailNotDisposable` \u2014 `EnsureOwnerEmailNotDisposable`** *(validation)*\nIf the email's domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailException`. Absent/domain-less email is left alone.\n\n**4. `ensurePostcode` \u2014 `EnsureOwnerPostcode`** *(validation)*\nIf a postcode is supplied it must be exactly 4 digits, and for a known-region city must fall in range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException`. Absent postcode / unknown-region city is left alone.\n\n**5. `adjustRegistrationDate` \u2014 `AdjustOwnerRegistrationDate`** *(side-effect)*\nRolls the registration date forward off Saturdays, Sundays, and listed 2026 public holidays to the next business day (mutates the owner).\n\n**6. `normalizeTelephone` \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** *(side-effect + validation)*\nRewrites the phone to E.164 (`+` keeps its country code; otherwise `+61` assumed and a leading `0` dropped; spaces/dashes/brackets stripped). Validates 8\u201315 digits, `+61` must have 9 national digits, `+1` must have 10 \u2192 else `InvalidTelephoneException`. Mutates the owner.\n\n**7. `normalizeAddress` \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerAddress`** *(side-effect + validation)*\nPrefers `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` when line1 is non-blank, else the flat `address`; each part trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, with `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE` expanded; sets `addressLine1` and the combined `address`. If neither address form is present \u2192 `InvalidAddressException`. Mutates the owner.\n\n**8. `ensureUniqueHousehold` \u2014 `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold`** *(side-effect)*\nAssigns the deterministic `householdId` (from last name + postcode). Despite the name, it never rejects.\n\n**9. `ensureUniqueIdentity` \u2014 `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity`** *(validation)*\nRejects if the full `IdentityKey` (normalized telephone + email + householdId) exactly matches an existing non-deleted owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException`. Scans all owners.\n\n**10. `ensureCityCapacity` \u2014 `EnsureCityHasCapacity`** *(validation)*\nRejects if the owner's city already holds \u226550 owners (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n**11. `ensureDailyCapacity` \u2014 `EnsureDailyRegistrationCapacity`** *(validation)*\nRejects if \u2265100 owners already share the (adjusted) `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyRegistrationLimitException`.\n\n**12. `assignMemberId` \u2014 `AssignOwnerMemberId`** *(side-effect)*\nSets `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (via `MemberId.of`), after phone/date are settled.\n\n**13. `deduplicateMemberId` \u2014 `DeduplicateOwnerMemberId`** *(side-effect)*\nIf that `memberId` already belongs to another owner, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2) to make it unique.\n\n**14. `countNamesakes` \u2014 `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`** *(side-effect)*\nSets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive; excludes this not-yet-saved owner).\n\n**15. `countHousehold` \u2014 `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize`** *(side-effect)*\nSets `householdSize` = 1 + existing owners sharing this `householdId`.\n\n**16. `save` \u2014 `SaveOwner`** *(side-effect)*\nPersists the owner (assigns its database id).\n\n**17. `record` \u2014 `RecordIdempotencyKey`** *(side-effect)*\nIf an `Idempotency-Key` header was present, stores `key \u2192 owner.id` in the static `SEEN` map (feeds step 1 on replay).\n\n**18. `audit` \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`** *(side-effect)*\nEmits two `AUDIT` log lines: a text line and a structured JSON `OWNER_CREATED` event (schema v2), incrementing a static sequence counter.\n\n**19. `notifyWelcome` \u2014 `NotifyOwnerWelcome`** *(side-effect)*\nEmits a `NOTIFY` \"welcome owner\" log line (enqueues the welcome notification).\n\n**20. `respond` \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(side-effect / response)*\nMaps to `OwnerDto`, then sets `bulkSignupWarning`, `contactPreference`, and `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (the duplicate check is **skipped** when the request's `sharesHousehold` is true). Responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes\n- The transaction spanning all steps commits once, at step 20.\n- Any thrown exception is mapped by the matching handler under `officefloor/escalation/` (e.g. the `Duplicate*`/`Invalid*`/`*Capacity*`/`RegistrationDateInFuture` exceptions \u2192 4xx responses), rather than persisting a partial owner.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging (observations, not changes): step 8's class is named `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold` and its Javadoc mentions \"capping membership level,\" but the code only assigns the `householdId` \u2014 it performs no uniqueness rejection or level capping. Likewise `EnsureUnique...` naming aside, the only real duplicate rejection is the consolidated identity check in step 9."
